\details{
\itemize{
\item \code{ECA()}: evolutionary centers algorithm.
\item \code{DE()}: differential evolution (strategies \code{"rand1"}, \code{"rand2"},
\code{"best1"}, \code{"randToBest1"} and \code{"best2"}).
\item \code{epsilonDE()}: the epsilon constrained differential evolution (named
with a Greek epsilon in Metaheuristics.jl).
\item \code{SHADE()}: success history based adaptive differential evolution.
\item \code{RDEx()}: the reconstructed differential evolution with elite based
mutation and adaptive memories.
\item \code{PSO()}: particle swarm optimization.
\item \code{ABC()}: artificial bee colony.
\item \code{SA()}: simulated annealing.
\item \code{WOA()}: whale optimization algorithm.
\item \code{CGSA()}: chaotic gravitational search algorithm.
\item \code{CSO()}: competitive swarm optimizer.
\item \code{GA()}: a genetic algorithm assembled from operators of
\link{Metaheuristics} (initializer, selection, crossover, mutation and
environmental selection); \code{BRKGA()} is the biased random key genetic
algorithm built from them.
\item \code{MCCGA()}: machine coded compact genetic algorithm, with a final
Hooke and Jeeves search.
}

ECA, DE, epsilonDE, SHADE, PSO, SA, CSO, GA and BRKGA accept the
constraints of the problem (\code{cons} with \code{lcons} and \code{ucons}), which become
the inequality and equality constraints of Metaheuristics.jl and are
handled by its feasibility rules. The \code{solve} arguments map as in
OptimizationMetaheuristics: \code{maxiters} to the number of iterations,
\code{maxtime} to the time limit, \code{abstol} to \code{f_tol}; every field of
\code{Metaheuristics$Options()} can be given too, and \code{use_initial = TRUE}
seeds the population with \code{u0}. The random numbers are R's: call
\code{\link[=set.seed]{set.seed()}} (or give \code{seed}) for reproducible runs.
